    "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 2791 experienced a gross prior year reserve release of GBP 16.1 million in 2020, representing a 5.0% reduction of its opening gross reserves. This favorable development was driven by several factors, including a GBP 5.4 million gross release from long-tail casualty classes, a GBP 4.5 million gross release from the short-tail account, and a GBP 6.2 million gross release from Auto and other miscellaneous specialty classes, with 60% of this attributed to better than expected performance on the Irish motor account (2012-16). Specific events contributing to the release include favorable legal rulings for Superstorm Sandy (2012) and a market-wide arbitration for a Canadian wildfire reinsurance contract (2015). However, some adverse development was noted, including a roughly 10% deterioration in gross Hurricane Irma (2017) losses and an increase in ultimate gross catastrophe losses for the 2017 events (Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria, and Californian Wildfires).",
